    "background_story": "Fabian was a contemplative soul, often lost in thought as he gazed at his navel. His friends and family would tease him about his tendency towards omphaloskepsis, but Fabian couldn't help it. He found solace in the quiet, introspective moments, searching for answers to life's mysteries within himself. As a philosophy student, Fabian was drawn to the ancient Greeks, who believed that the navel was the center of the universe. He saw parallels between this idea and his own quest for self-discovery. Fabian's introspection led him to develop a unique perspective on the world, one that valued mindfulness and inner wisdom. Though some saw his navel-gazing as quirky, Fabian knew that it was a source of strength, allowing him to navigate life's complexities with greater clarity and purpose.",
